{"id":"word:hebrew:H2930","type":"word","title":"טָמֵא","subtitle":"H2930 • Hebrew word","simple":{"meaning":"to be foul , especially in a ceremial or moral sense (contaminated)","inThisVerse":"The selected word is tied to טָמֵא (H2930) in the Hebrew source text. Part of speech: v.","whyItMatters":"This word appears 162 times in the Hebrew Bible, so BibleIQ can compare how Scripture uses it across multiple passages.","summary":"טָמֵא (ṭâmêʼ) means to be foul , especially in a ceremial or moral sense (contaminated) First listed occurrence: 2Chr 36 14."},"evidence":{"originalLanguage":{"source":"hebrew","word":"טָמֵא","transliteration":"ṭâmêʼ","pronunciation":"taw-may'","strong":"H2930","lemmaId":"hebrew:H2930","partOfSpeech":"v","forms":["וְ/טָמֵ֥א","יִטְמָ֖א","יִטְמָֽא","יִטְמָ֥א","יִטְמָ֑א"],"morphs":[["HVqi3ms",34],["HC/Vqq3ms",22],["HVpp3ms",9],["HR/Vqc",7],["HVNp3fs",7],["HC/Vpq3ms",6],["HVti3ms",5],["HVti3mp",4],["HC/Vpq3ms/Sp3ms",4],["HC/Vpw3mp",3]]},"definitions":{"short":"to be foul , especially in a ceremial or moral sense (contaminated)","usage":"defile (self), pollute (self), be (make, make self, pronounce) unclean, × utterly.","full":"H2930. tame I. טָמֵא verb be or become unclean (Late Hebrew Pi`el pollute (ceremonially); Aramaic טְמָא and especially derivatives, Pa`el pollute ; see RS K 307 ff. ) — Qal Perfect 3masculine singular ׳ט Lev 11:25 22 t.; 3 feminine singular טָֽמְאָה 12:2 2 t.; 2 feminine singular טָמֵאת Ezek 22:4 ; plural טָֽמְאוּ Lev 15:18 ; Imperfect יִטְמָא 5:3 34t.; 3 feminine singular תִּטְמָא 12:2 4 t.; plural יִטְמְאוּ Psa 106:39 ; Infinitive טָמְאָה Lev 15:32 6 t.; — be or become unclean: 1 sexually , with בְּ Lev 18:20 , 23 (H), Ezek 23:17 ; the land Lev 18:25 , 27 (H). 2 religiously, with idols Ezek 22:3 ; with בְ 22:4 ; with necromancers Lev 19:31 (H); by sacrificing children to idols Psa 106:39 . 3 ceremonially, by contact with carcasses of unclean animals Lev 11:24 , 27 , 28 , 31 , 32 , 33 , 34 (twice in verse); 11:35-36 , 40 (P); any carcass 17:15 (H); eating of a carcass 22:8 (H); by issues 15:4 , 9 , 20 (twice in verse); 15:24 , 27 , 32 (P); by contact with an unclean man 5:3 ; 15:4 (P), 22:5 (H), or thing 22:6 (H); by leprosy 13:14 , 46 ; 14:36 , 46 (P); by contact with the dead Num 6:12 ; 19:20 (P), Ezek 44:25 , or with one unclean by such contact Num 19:22 (P), Hag 2:13 (twice in verse); by contact with creeping things Lev 22:5 (H); certain animals were always unclean 11:26-27 , (P). In ordinary cases of uncleanness הערב עד טמא unclean till even 11:24-25 , 27 , 28 , 31 , 32 , 39 , 40 (twice in verse); 14:46 ; 15:5 ; 15:6 ; 15:7 ; 15:8 ; 15:10 (twice in verse); 15:11 , 16 , 17 , 18 , 19 , 21 , 22 , 23 , 27 ; Num 19:7 ; 19:8 ; 19:10 ; 19:21 ; 19:22 (all P), Lev 17:15 ; 22:6 (H); but uncleanness lasted 7 days for woman bearings a son 12:2 (twice in verse) (P), for lying with woman having an issue 15:24 (P), or one coming in contact with the dead Num 19:11 , 14 , 16 (P); it lasted 14 days for a woman bearing a daughter Lev 12:5 (P). Niph`al Perfect 3masculine singular נִטְמָא Hosea 5:3 ; 6:10 ; 3 feminine singular נִטְמְאָה Num 5:27-28 , נִטְמָ֑אָה 5:13 5 t.; 1 singular נִטְמֵאתִי Jer 2:23 ; 2 masculine plural נִטְמֵתֶם Lev 11:43 ( א omitted by scribal error; but Ges and others derive from טמה ), etc. + 4 t. perfect; Participle plural נִטְמְאִים Ezek 20:30-31 , &#8212; defile oneself, be defiled: 1 sexually , Lev 18:24 (H), Num 5:13-14 , (twice in verse); 5:20 , 27 , 28 , 29 (P). 2 by idolatry conceived as whoredom Hosea 5:3 ; 6:10 ; Jer 2:23 ; Ezek 20:30-31 , 43 ; 23:7 , 13 , 30 . 3 ceremonially, by eating creeping things Lev 11:43 . 4 be regarded as unclean (compare Pi`el 4 ), probably נִטְמִינִוּ Job 18:3 we are accounted as unclean ; metal. from; on another view see טמה . Pi`el Perfect טִמֵּא Gen 34:5 15 t.; suffix טִמְּאוֺ Lev 13:8 3 t.; 2 feminine singular טִמֵּאת Ezek 5:11 , etc. + 7 t. Perfect; Imperfect יְטַמֵּא 2Kin 23:8 , etc. + 12 t. Imperfect; Imperative plural טַמְּאוּ Ezek 9:7 ; Infinitive טַמֵּא Lev 13:44 2 t.; suffix טַמְּאָם 15:31 , etc. + 4 t. Infinitive; — defile: 1 sexually Gen 34:5 , 13 , 27 (R), Ezek 18:6 , 11 , 15 ; 22:11 ; 33:26 ; the land by sexual impurities of the people Lev 18:28 (H); Israel by spiritual whoredom Ezek 23:17 . 2 religiously: the land by bloodshed Num 35:34 (P); by allowing the dead body of the murderer to hang on the tree over night Deut 21:23 ; by idolatry Jer 2:7 ; Ezek 36:17-18 , Israel defiled the sacred places by the sacrifice of children Lev 20:3 (H), Ezek 23:38 , and God defiled him thereby 20:26 ; he defileth the sacred places by idolatry 2Chr 36:14 ; Jer 7:30 = 32:34 , Ezek 5:11 ; the holy name of ׳י 43:7-8 , Josiah defiled the idolatrous places of worship by destroying them and making them unfit for use 2Kin 23:8 , 10 , 13 , 16 ; of Israel defiling idolatrous images Isa 30:22 , and the nations the temple of God Psa 79:1 . 3 ceremonially: by ceremonial uncleanness, the sacred places Lev 15:31 ; Num 19:13 , 20 (P); the camp 5:3 (P); the temple by dead bodies Ezek 9:7 ; the Nazirite's head of separation by a death occurring in his presence Num 6:9 (P); the people defile themselves ( נפשׁתיכם ) by creeping things Lev 11:44 (P). 4 pronounce or declare ceremonially unclean: the leper Lev 13:3 , 8 , 11 , 15 , 20 , 22 , 25 , 27 , 30 , 44 (twice in verse); 13:59 (P); unclean animals 20:25 (H). Pu`al Participle מְטֻמָּאָה לֹא נַפְשִׁי Ezek 4:14 myself is not polluted. Hithpa`el Imperfect יִטַּמָּא Lev 21:1 4 t.; plural יִטַּמְּאוּ Ezek 14:11 ; 37:23 ; יִטַּמָּ֑אוּ Hosea 9:4 ; Ezek 44:25 , etc. + 6 t. Imperfect — reflexive, defile oneself: by eating of an unaccepted peace-offering Hosea 9:4 ; with בְּ Lev 18:24 , 30 (H), 11:43 (P), Ezek 14:11 ; 20:7 , 18 ; 37:23 ; with לְ for a dead person Lev 21:1 , 3 , 11 (H), Num 6:7 (P); by Lev 11:24 (P); without preposition 21:4 (H), Ezek 44:25 . Hothpa`al Perfect חֻטַּמָּ֑אָה אֲשֶׁר אַחֲרֵי Deut 24:4 after that she has been defiled (sexually); on form see Ges § 54 . 3. טָמְאָה noun feminine uncleanness ( טָֽמְאָה , Bear, seems to rest upon a misinterpretation of the form) Micah 2:10 (so Thes MV SS); of ethical uncleanness, from wrong-doing.","rootNote":"a primitive root;","sources":["MorphHB occurrences","Strong Hebrew Dictionary","Brown-Driver-Briggs"]},"firstMention":"2Chr 36 14","keyReferences":["2Chr 36 14","2Kgs 23 8","2Kgs 23 10","2Kgs 23 13","2Kgs 23 16","Deut 21 23","Deut 24 4","Ezek 4 14"],"related":{"people":[],"places":[],"concepts":[],"events":[]},"occurrenceCount":162,"occurrences":[{"reference":"2Chr 36 14","book":"2Chr","chapter":36,"verse":14,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"וַֽ/יְטַמְּאוּ֙","source":"hebrew","morph":"HC/Vpw3mp"},{"reference":"2Kgs 23 8","book":"2Kgs","chapter":23,"verse":8,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"וַ/יְטַמֵּ֣א","source":"hebrew","morph":"HC/Vpw3ms"},{"reference":"2Kgs 23 10","book":"2Kgs","chapter":23,"verse":10,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"וְ/טִמֵּ֣א","source":"hebrew","morph":"HC/Vpp3ms"},{"reference":"2Kgs 23 13","book":"2Kgs","chapter":23,"verse":13,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"טִמֵּ֖א","source":"hebrew","morph":"HVpp3ms"},{"reference":"2Kgs 23 16","book":"2Kgs","chapter":23,"verse":16,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"וַֽ/יְטַמְּאֵ֑/הוּ","source":"hebrew","morph":"HC/Vpw3ms/Sp3ms"},{"reference":"Deut 21 23","book":"Deut","chapter":21,"verse":23,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"תְטַמֵּא֙","source":"hebrew","morph":"HVpi2ms"},{"reference":"Deut 24 4","book":"Deut","chapter":24,"verse":4,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"הֻטַּמָּ֔אָה","source":"hebrew","morph":"HVup3fs"},{"reference":"Ezek 4 14","book":"Ezek","chapter":4,"verse":14,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"מְטֻמָּאָ֑ה","source":"hebrew","morph":"HVPsfsa"},{"reference":"Ezek 5 11","book":"Ezek","chapter":5,"verse":11,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"טִמֵּ֔את","source":"hebrew","morph":"HVpp2fs"},{"reference":"Ezek 9 7","book":"Ezek","chapter":9,"verse":7,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"טַמְּא֣וּ","source":"hebrew","morph":"HVpv2mp"},{"refere